  "scope": "Sequential predecessor gating for the memory journal and explicit durable completion. Native owners retain storage observations, indexed claim selection, lease admission and the outer transaction.",
  "limitations": [
    "Frozen pre-extraction gate bodies come from 63df912e and do not call migrated gate policy. Native fixtures, storage and public dispatch/completion machinery remain shared.",
    "The 2520 memory cases cover fourteen execution-order labels, two owner states, nine predecessor classes, five target positions and two acknowledgement states. This is a scalar gate matrix, not seventy operation implementations.",
    "The 432 SQLite comparisons cover four sources, three lifecycle stages, twelve mutations and three target tokens. Corrupt fixtures exercise original fault precedence and are not admitted recovery checkpoints; production constraints are unchanged.",
    "Twelve memory and twelve durable public group shapes cover sequential and parallel tail, capture, multi-capture and conditional paths. Durable paths reopen after the first acknowledgement and finish without redispatch.",
    "Memory keeps closed-owner refusal and Step::Done-only predecessor classification with lazy prefix reads. SQLite keeps its original stored-state EXISTS observation, including different missing-row and closed-owner behavior. These differences are preserved, not promoted as host-neutral recovery semantics.",
    "The borrowed-transaction test observes an uncommitted predecessor update through the original outer transaction without writing or committing, and rollback restores the original refusal.",
    "Indexed claim SQL remains in the native atomic lease transaction. The adapter adds no candidate materialization, per-candidate SQL, retries, decoding, payload admission or independent commit.",
    "No new Linux, remote CI, live GUI, actual exported-source execution, full host-neutral durable recovery, power-loss, disk-full, multi-host race or performance evidence is claimed."
  ],
